.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt NVMFD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvmfd
.Nd NVMe over Fabrics target daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dFfGg
.Oo Fl a Ar address Oc Ns ...
.Op Fl H Ar maxh2cdata
.Op Fl P Ar discovery_port
.Op Fl p Ar io_port
.Op Fl t Ar transport
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon accepts NVMe over Fabrics connections over TCP for the
.Xr nvmft 4D
target port provider.
It listens on two ports.
On the I/O port it completes the Connect command of each new queue and
then hands the connection to
.Xr nvmft 4D ,
which serves the subsystem's namespaces from then on.
On the discovery port it runs a discovery controller whose log page
lists every subsystem created with
.Xr nvmfadm 8 ,
once for each address that the I/O port listens on.
.Pp
The daemon is normally run by the
.Xr smf 7
service
.Sy svc:/system/nvmf/target:default .
The service first creates the subsystems that
.Xr nvmfadm 8
has saved and then starts
.Nm .
Its
.Sy config/discovery_port ,
.Sy config/io_port
and
.Sy config/listen_addresses
properties supply the
.Fl P ,
.Fl p
and
.Fl a
options.
Disabling the service stops new connections.
Queues already handed to
.Xr nvmft 4D
stay connected until their subsystem is taken offline or deleted.
.Pp
.Nm
must be started with all privileges.
Once it has opened the
.Xr nvmft 4D
control node and bound its ports it runs as user
.Sy daemon
with the basic privilege set and
.Sy sys_devices .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ar
.It Fl a Ar address
Listen on
.Ar address
only.
The option may be repeated.
By default
.Nm
listens on every IPv4 and IPv6 address of the system.
.It Fl d
Stay in the foreground and write log messages to standard error
instead of
.Xr syslog 3C .
.It Fl F
Permit hosts to turn off submission queue flow control.
.It Fl f
Stay in the foreground.
.It Fl G
Permit data digests.
.It Fl g
Permit header digests.
.It Fl H Ar maxh2cdata
The largest data payload, in bytes, that a host may send in one PDU.
The value must be a multiple of 4 and at least 4096.
The default is 262144.
.It Fl P Ar discovery_port
The TCP port of the discovery controller.
The default is 8009.
.It Fl p Ar io_port
The TCP port for I/O controllers.
The default is 4420.
.It Fl t Ar transport
The transport.
Only
.Sy tcp
is supported.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
.Nm
does not authenticate hosts and does not encrypt.
In-band authentication (DH-HMAC-CHAP) and TLS are not implemented.
Any host that can reach the ports can read the discovery log and
connect to any subsystem.
Use
.Fl a
and packet filtering to limit which hosts can reach the daemon, and
STMF host groups and views to limit which logical units a host NQN can
see; see
.Xr stmfadm 8 .
A host NQN is whatever the host claims and is not proof of identity.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Sy Example 1
Enabling the target service on one address
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# svccfg -s svc:/system/nvmf/target:default \e
    setprop config/listen_addresses = astring: 192.168.10.5
# svcadm refresh svc:/system/nvmf/target:default
# svcadm enable svc:/system/nvmf/target:default
.Ed
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
The command line interface of
.Nm
is
.Sy Uncommitted .
